{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Polynomial Multiplication.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Polynomial Multiplication.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"polynomial multiplication polynomial multiplication","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Polynomial Multiplication.md","fileName":"Polynomial Multiplication.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Polynomial Multiplication","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 23:41\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Polynomial and Rational Expressions]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Polynomial and Rational Expressions","Laws of Exponents","FOIL Method","algebraessentials.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Polynomial Multiplication.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Polynomial Multiplication.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"polynomial multiplication polynomial multiplication","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Polynomial Multiplication.md","fileName":"Polynomial Multiplication.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Polynomial Multiplication","heading":"Polynomial Multiplication","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Polynomial multiplication distributes every term of one polynomial across every term of the other. Coefficients multiply, powers with a common base combine through the [[Laws of Exponents]], and like terms are collected after all products are formed.\n\nThe method works for any number of terms. For two binomials, the [[FOIL Method]] is a mnemonic for the same complete distribution. An omitted cross-product changes the result, which is why ((a+b)^2) equals (a^2+2ab+b^2) rather than (a^2+b^2).","tags":["baby"],"links":["Polynomial and Rational Expressions","Laws of Exponents","FOIL Method","algebraessentials.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Polynomial Multip